; E# hardware test pack. Run from this drawer:  Execute RunAll
; (AmigaDOS comments start with a semicolon at the beginning of a line only.)
; Writes one file per program into results/ and a summary in SUMMARY.txt.
; Self-checking programs print "ok name" or "FAIL name". screen, aga, rtg, sound, cards and rummy
; also show a picture or play sound: look and listen (see README.txt), press Esc or wait.

FailAt 21
Echo "E# hardware test pack" >SUMMARY.txt
Type BUILD >>SUMMARY.txt
Echo "" >>SUMMARY.txt
hwinfo >results/hwinfo.txt
Type results/hwinfo.txt >>SUMMARY.txt
Echo "" >>SUMMARY.txt

Echo "hello"
hello >results/hello.txt
Echo "phase2"
phase2 >results/phase2.txt
Echo "memory"
memory >results/memory.txt
Echo "generics"
generics >results/generics.txt
Echo "properties"
properties >results/properties.txt
Echo "operators"
operators >results/operators.txt
Echo "language"
language >results/language.txt
Echo "collections"
collections >results/collections.txt
Echo "inherit"
inherit >results/inherit.txt
Echo "lambdas"
lambdas >results/lambdas.txt
Echo "linq"
linq >results/linq.txt
Echo "refs"
refs >results/refs.txt
Echo "screen (a card picture appears for a few seconds)"
screen >results/screen.txt
Echo "aga (a 256 colour picture appears for a few seconds)"
aga >results/aga.txt
Echo "rtg"
rtg >results/rtg.txt
Echo "sound (you should hear tones)"
sound >results/sound.txt
Echo "controls (timer and joystick: move the stick in port 1 if you like)"
controls >results/controls.txt
Echo "keys (a blank screen: press A within 10 seconds)"
keys >results/keys.txt
Echo "dates (dates and case-insensitive text)"
dates >results/dates.txt
Echo "cards (play a round; Esc quits, or leave it for 10 seconds)"
cards >results/cards.txt
Echo "rummy (play a turn; Esc quits, or leave it for 10 seconds)"
rummy >results/rummy.txt

Echo "Lines with FAIL (nothing listed below is good):" >>SUMMARY.txt
Search results ALL "FAIL " QUIET >>SUMMARY.txt
Echo "" >>SUMMARY.txt
Echo "Done. Send SUMMARY.txt, the results drawer and the answers in README.txt (section 3) back."
